{"candidates":[{"claim":"Greedy single-comparator removal from Batcher's odd-even mergesort network for n=13 (48 comparators) will get stuck above 45 comparators, discriminating the 'structural barrier' hypothesis (predicts stall >45, meaning 45-nets require fundamentally different structure) from the 'redundant Batcher' hypothesis (predicts reaching ≤45, meaning the best-known 45-net is extractable as a subnetwork of Batcher's construction). The structural barrier hypothesis is expected to be supported.","counterconditions":["If greedy pruning reaches ≤45 comparators, the 'redundant Batcher' hypothesis is supported instead and the structural barrier claim is falsified — the 45-net would be a subnetwork of Batcher's construction, implying no novel structure is needed.","If the Batcher implementation is incorrect (the generated network does not sort all 8192 binary vectors), the entire experiment is invalid and all pruning results are void.","If greedy pruning order matters (different removal orders yield different final sizes), the single-order result underestimates removable comparators; a systematic search over removal orders would be needed to fully discriminate.","If verify_sorting has an implementation bug causing false positives (network that does not actually sort passes), pruning results are unreliable and the discrimination is void.","If the final pruned size is exactly 46, the result is ambiguous: it neither confirms structural barrier nor redundancy decisively, since a different pruning heuristic might reach 45."],"evidence_refs":[{"block":"680b4c459d28bf7a","quote":"S(n) denotes the minimum comparator count of any n-input sorting network."},{"block":"b01150a3ae43d8f6","quote":"The 0-1 principle: a comparator network on n channels sorts ALL inputs if and only if it sorts every input drawn from {0,1}^n."},{"block":"6050cf69f391fa33","quote":"Consequently a 13-input candidate is verified by running all 2^13 = 8192 binary vectors through it"},{"block":"843819388191d0e9","quote":"A candidate network is a list of (i, j) pairs with 0 <= i < j < 13."},{"block":"4f053d098dcef347","quote":"A simulation that cannot discriminate between rival predictions is weight, not evidence."},{"block":"8a7a7d8f89f48b3e","quote":"S(n) is PROVEN for n up to 12"}],"mechanism":"The simulation generates Batcher's odd-even mergesort network for n=13 using the standard iterative formulation (p=1..n; k=p..1; inner loop over channels), yielding ~48 comparators. It verifies the network sorts all 2^13=8192 binary vectors via the 0-1 principle. Then it greedily prunes: iteratively try removing each comparator (right-to-left), and keep the removal if the reduced network still sorts all 8192 vectors. Repeat until no single removal preserves sorting. Final comparator count discriminates the two hypotheses. Full Python code:\n\n```python\ndef batcher_network(n):\n    comps = []\n    p = 1\n    while p < n:\n        k = p\n        while k > 0:\n            j = k % p\n            while j < n - k:\n                for i in range(k):\n                    if ((i + j) // p) % 2 == 0:\n                        if i + j + k < n:\n                            a, b = i + j, i + j + k\n                            comps.append((min(a, b), max(a, b)))\n                j += 2 * k\n            k //= 2\n        p *= 2\n    return comps\n\ndef verify_sorting(comps, n):\n    for mask in range(1 << n):\n        arr = [(mask >> ch) & 1 for ch in range(n)]\n        for (a, b) in comps:\n            if arr[a] > arr[b]:\n                arr[a], arr[b] = arr[b], arr[a]\n        for ch in range(n - 1):\n            if arr[ch] > arr[ch + 1]:\n                return False\n    return True\n\ndef greedy_prune(comps, n):\n    current = list(comps)\n    changed = True\n    while changed:\n        changed = False\n        for idx in range(len(current) - 1, -1, -1):\n            trial = current[:idx] + current[idx + 1:]\n            if verify_sorting(trial, n):\n                current = trial\n                changed = True\n    return current\n\nn = 13\nnetwork = batcher_network(n)\nassert verify_sorting(network, n), \"Batcher network does not sort!\"\npruned = greedy_prune(network, n)\nassert verify_sorting(pruned, n)\nremoved = len(network) - len(pruned)\nprint(f\"Batcher: {len(network)}, Pruned: {len(pruned)}, Removed: {removed}\")\nif len(pruned) <= 44:\n    print(\"OUTCOME: <=44 — REDUNDANCY hypothesis supported\")\nelif len(pruned) == 45:\n    print(\"OUTCOME: ==45 — matches known best via subnetwork extraction\")\nelse:\n    print(f\"OUTCOME: {len(pruned)}>45 — STRUCTURAL BARRIER hypothesis supported\")\n```","optional_refs":["src-c684127f981a8a8c1d5e0739c804e68436eebc3d"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["src-c684127f981a8a8c1d5e0739c804e68436eebc3d"],"search_signal":"productive"},"typicality":0.55}],"simulation_proposals":[]}